let's leave water out of the discussion. that was just the lunatic musing
of a disgruntled nethack hacker, nothing consequential (i took a vow never
to use smileys again)...

the thing that makes nethackers sick about the eating code add-ons is the
fact that you waste moves collapsing under your load and then dropping a
corpse that you never intended tp pickup. of course, there's other problems
like the inconsistent behavior between eating uninterrupted and eating while
interrupted and the resume eating stuff when you've changed your mind about
what you want to eat next. if the game must pick up a food item that you've
decided to eat off the ground then the game should drop the food item when
you get interrupted (special case shops?). when you say "e"at you expect to
be presented a menu and it is usually a surprise to resume eating without
confirmation. you also expect that if you could enjoy a meal without
interruption that if you were interrupted and returned to eating within
a reasonable amount of time that the experience would be similar to the
uninterrupted situation. you don't expect to choke over your food merely
because you were interrupted while eating. these are reasonable expectations
that the present code doesn't properly satisfy. it appears that patch 6
will fix all that ...

what do we sacrifice to keep the developers happy? ...

